IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ucpr-time`
IMPORT `ucpr-offers-costs`

-- Uniform Civil Procedure Rules 2005 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in ucpr-offers-costs.l4. Every
-- expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (with a calendar for the days of the week); none was copied
-- from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases -- offers, costs and interest`

`d` MEANS `the date`
`no holidays` MEANS LIST `d` 1 1 1900

`SC` MEANS `the Supreme Court`
`DC` MEANS `the District Court`
`LC` MEANS `the Local Court`

`mine` MEANS `I made the offer`
`theirs` MEANS `the defendant made the offer`

`own terms` MEANS `the accepted offer's own terms about costs apply`
`42.13A(2)` MEANS `the defendant pays my costs on the ordinary basis up to the time the offer was made`
`42.13A(3)` MEANS `I pay the defendant's costs on the ordinary basis up to the time the offer was made`
`42.14` MEANS `the defendant pays my costs, on the ordinary basis and then on the indemnity basis`
`42.15` MEANS `the defendant pays my costs on the ordinary basis up to the switch, and I pay its costs on the indemnity basis after it`
`42.15A` MEANS `I pay the defendant's costs, on the ordinary basis and then on the indemnity basis`
`no offer order` MEANS `the offer rules give no costs order, so the general rule applies: costs follow the event unless the court orders otherwise`
`not money` MEANS `not worked out here: the offer and the judgment are not both for a sum of money`

§§ `r 20.26(5) -- closing date`

-- Arguments: day of offer, trial date set, trial date.
-- Offer 1 March 2025, trial 1 May 2025: exactly two months before, so at least 28 days: 29 March.
#ASSERT `What is the earliest closing date for my offer` (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 5 2025) EQUALS JUST (`d` 29 3 2025)
#ASSERT `What is the earliest closing date for my offer` (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 2 5 2025) EQUALS JUST (`d` 29 3 2025)
-- Trial 30 April: less than two months; and no trial date set (fork F12): "reasonable in the circumstances" (NOTHING).
#ASSERT `What is the earliest closing date for my offer` (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 30 4 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is the earliest closing date for my offer` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `r 20.26(2), (3), (5) -- a valid offer`

-- Arguments: identifies claim and orders, part only, says what happens to the rest, includes costs, defendant's offer
-- with a costs sum, accordance statement, interim payment, says whether in addition, period specified, day of offer,
-- closing date, trial date set, trial date, closing date reasonable.
-- A complete offer made 1 March 2025, trial 1 June, closing 29 March: valid; closing 28 March: one day short.
#ASSERT `Does the offer meet rule 20.26` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 29 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the offer meet rule 20.26` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 28 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Trial 30 April (less than two months away): the closing date must be reasonable (the court's judgment).
#ASSERT `Does the offer meet rule 20.26` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 30 4 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the offer meet rule 20.26` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 30 4 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Each requirement missed: proposed orders, part offer without a statement on the rest, costs included, no accordance
-- statement, interim payment not addressed, no period of acceptance.
#ASSERT `Does the offer meet rule 20.26` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 29 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the offer meet rule 20.26` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 29 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the offer meet rule 20.26` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 29 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the offer meet rule 20.26` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 29 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the offer meet rule 20.26` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 29 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the offer meet rule 20.26` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 29 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the offer meet rule 20.26` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 29 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the offer meet rule 20.26` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 29 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the offer meet rule 20.26` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 29 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `r 20.26(4) -- notice that I cannot assess the offer`

-- Arguments: lacking particulars, received, notice day, weekends closed, other closed days.
-- Received Friday 7 March: 14 days end Friday 21 March; notice on 22 March is late.
#ASSERT `Can I give notice that I cannot assess the offer` TRUE (`d` 7 3 2025) (`d` 21 3 2025) TRUE `no holidays` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I give notice that I cannot assess the offer` TRUE (`d` 7 3 2025) (`d` 22 3 2025) TRUE `no holidays` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I give notice that I cannot assess the offer` FALSE (`d` 7 3 2025) (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE `no holidays` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Received Saturday 1 March: 15 March is a Saturday, so Monday 17 March.
#ASSERT `Can I give notice that I cannot assess the offer` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 17 3 2025) TRUE `no holidays` EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `r 20.26(8), 20.28, 20.29 -- payment under an accepted offer`

-- Arguments: I accepted, accepted on, own time, its days, weekends closed, other closed days, paid, paid on, today.
-- Accepted Monday 3 March 2025: 28 days end Monday 31 March.
#ASSERT `Has the defendant paid under the accepted offer` TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) FALSE 0 TRUE `no holidays` TRUE (`d` 31 3 2025) (`d` 5 4 2025) EQUALS `paid or done in time`
#ASSERT `Has the defendant paid under the accepted offer` TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) FALSE 0 TRUE `no holidays` TRUE (`d` 1 4 2025) (`d` 5 4 2025) EQUALS `not paid in time: I may withdraw my acceptance, or elect judgment on the offer's terms or to have the defence struck out`
#ASSERT `Has the defendant paid under the accepted offer` TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) FALSE 0 TRUE `no holidays` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 31 3 2025) EQUALS `not yet due`
#ASSERT `Has the defendant paid under the accepted offer` FALSE (`d` 3 3 2025) FALSE 0 TRUE `no holidays` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 4 2025) EQUALS `not paid in time: I may elect judgment on the offer's terms or to have the defence struck out`
-- The offer gives 14 days: they end Monday 17 March; payment on 18 March is late.
#ASSERT `Has the defendant paid under the accepted offer` TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) TRUE 14 TRUE `no holidays` TRUE (`d` 18 3 2025) (`d` 20 3 2025) EQUALS `not paid in time: I may withdraw my acceptance, or elect judgment on the offer's terms or to have the defence struck out`
#ASSERT `Has the defendant paid under the accepted offer` TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) TRUE 14 TRUE `no holidays` TRUE (`d` 17 3 2025) (`d` 20 3 2025) EQUALS `paid or done in time`
-- Accepted Saturday 1 March: 29 March is a Saturday, so payment on Monday 31 March is in time.
#ASSERT `Has the defendant paid under the accepted offer` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE 0 TRUE `no holidays` TRUE (`d` 31 3 2025) (`d` 5 4 2025) EQUALS `paid or done in time`
-- A payment dated after "today" has not been made yet.
#ASSERT `Has the defendant paid under the accepted offer` TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) FALSE 0 TRUE `no holidays` TRUE (`d` 30 3 2025) (`d` 20 3 2025) EQUALS `not yet due`

§§ `r 42.13A-42.17 -- costs after an offer`

-- Arguments: who made it, accepted, accepted offer provided for costs, proposed judgment for me, I obtained judgment,
-- both money, offer amount, judgment amount, post-offer interest, willing-and-able asked, court satisfied.
-- Accepted offers (r 42.13A).
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `theirs` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 50000 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `own terms`
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `theirs` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE 50000 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `42.13A(2)`
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `mine` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `42.13A(3)`
-- My offer of $100,000 not accepted (r 42.14): judgment of $100,000 is no less favourable; $99,999 is.
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `mine` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100000 100000 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `42.14`
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `mine` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100000 99999 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no offer order`
-- r 42.16: $105,000 including $6,000 interest after the offer day counts as $99,000; with $5,000, $100,000.
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `mine` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100000 105000 6000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no offer order`
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `mine` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100000 105000 5000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `42.14`
-- I lost: r 42.14 does not apply.
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `mine` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100000 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no offer order`
-- r 42.17(3): asked to show willing and able; court not satisfied: r 42.14 does not apply; satisfied: it does.
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `mine` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100000 120000 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no offer order`
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `mine` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100000 120000 0 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `42.14`
-- The defendant's offer of $50,000 not accepted: judgment of $50,000 or $40,000 is no more favourable (r 42.15); $50,001
-- is more favourable (no offer order).
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `theirs` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 50000 50000 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `42.15`
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `theirs` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 50000 40000 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `42.15`
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `theirs` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 50000 50001 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no offer order`
-- r 42.16 works for the defendant too: $52,000 with $3,000 post-offer interest counts as $49,000 (r 42.15).
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `theirs` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 50000 52000 3000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `42.15`
-- I lost against the defendant's offer: r 42.15A.
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `theirs` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 50000 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `42.15A`
-- r 42.17(3) names only r 42.14 and 42.15: r 42.15A still applies; r 42.15 does not (finding 5).
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `theirs` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 50000 0 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `42.15A`
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `theirs` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 50000 40000 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no offer order`
-- Terms not both for money: not worked out here.
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the offer` `theirs` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 50000 40000 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not money`

-- Arguments: day of offer, first day of trial. Offer 10 March, trial 1 April: from the beginning of 11 March; offer on
-- the first day of trial: from 11 am the next day; offer the day before trial: from the beginning of the first day.
#ASSERT `From when do indemnity costs run` (`d` 10 3 2025) (`d` 1 4 2025) EQUALS `from the beginning of` (`d` 11 3 2025)
#ASSERT `From when do indemnity costs run` (`d` 31 3 2025) (`d` 1 4 2025) EQUALS `from the beginning of` (`d` 1 4 2025)
#ASSERT `From when do indemnity costs run` (`d` 1 4 2025) (`d` 1 4 2025) EQUALS `from 11 am on` (`d` 2 4 2025)
#ASSERT `From when do indemnity costs run` (`d` 2 4 2025) (`d` 1 4 2025) EQUALS `from 11 am on` (`d` 3 4 2025)

§§ `r 42.20 -- dismissal and striking out`

#ASSERT `Who pays the costs on dismissal or striking out` `my proceedings, or part of them, were dismissed` FALSE EQUALS `I pay the defendant's costs, to the extent the proceedings were dismissed`
#ASSERT `Who pays the costs on dismissal or striking out` `the defence, or part of it, was struck out` FALSE EQUALS `the defendant pays my costs of the matters on which the defence was struck out`
#ASSERT `Who pays the costs on dismissal or striking out` `the defence, or part of it, was struck out` TRUE EQUALS `the court's order governs`

§§ `r 42.34, 42.35 -- the lower court costs rule`

-- Arguments: court, defamation, against all defendants, amount, otherwise entitled, could have started lower, court
-- satisfied it was warranted.
#ASSERT `Does the lower court costs rule stop my costs order` `SC` FALSE TRUE 499999 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the lower court costs rule stop my costs order` `SC` FALSE TRUE 500000 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the lower court costs rule stop my costs order` `SC` FALSE TRUE 499999 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the lower court costs rule stop my costs order` `SC` TRUE TRUE 499999 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the lower court costs rule stop my costs order` `SC` FALSE FALSE 499999 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the lower court costs rule stop my costs order` `SC` FALSE TRUE 499999 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the lower court costs rule stop my costs order` `SC` FALSE TRUE 499999 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the lower court costs rule stop my costs order` `DC` FALSE TRUE 39999 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the lower court costs rule stop my costs order` `DC` FALSE TRUE 40000 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- r 42.35 has no defamation exception: a District Court defamation judgment below $40,000 is caught (finding 6).
#ASSERT `Does the lower court costs rule stop my costs order` `DC` TRUE TRUE 39999 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the lower court costs rule stop my costs order` `LC` FALSE TRUE 5000 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `r 36.7 -- interest`

#ASSERT `What is the interest rate on my judgment` 4.35 EQUALS 10.35
#ASSERT `What is the interest rate on my judgment` 0.1 EQUALS 6.1
#ASSERT `Can the court order interest up to judgment` `LC` 999 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the court order interest up to judgment` `LC` 1000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the court order interest up to judgment` `DC` 500 EQUALS NOTHING
